---
description: Use when the user asks for a chart, plot, graph, diagram, flowchart, UML, Gantt chart, Sankey diagram, dashboard or user-interface mockup. Draw it with the nymph MCP tools (render_chart) and look at the image.
alwaysApply: false
---

Draw charts and diagrams with nymph. Do not write the YAML from memory:
call `example_chart` with the element type you will use to get a working
source, call `chart_schema` for the fields of each element type you add,
then call `render_chart` and look at the PNG it returns. The nymph skill
and the nymph MCP server's instructions give the source format. When the
user wants the chart kept, pass `output_path` (a `.png`) and keep the YAML.

For a diagram (flowchart, sequence, class, state, ER, Gantt, mind map,
...) you may write mermaid instead: `render_chart` takes it as `source`
and draws it. Revise the mermaid until the user is satisfied, then call
`convert_chart` to get the nymph YAML and make further changes there.
